  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "M/S Elavankudy Tea Co vs Food Safety Officer on 4 June, 2019 Author: V Raja Vijayaraghavan Bench: V Raja Vijayaraghavan In The High Court Of Kerala At Ernakulam Present The Honourable Mr. Justice Raja Vijayaraghavan V Tuesday, The 04Th Day Of June 2019 / 14Th Jyaishta, 1941 Crl.M.C. No.3818 Of 2019 Against The C.C. No.2564/2014 Of The Judicial First Class Magistrate Court, Wadakkancherry Petitioner/4Th Accused : M/S Elavankudy Tea Co., 9/151A6, Police Station Road, Devala P.O., Gudallur, Nilgiri District, Pin-643 270, Represented By Its Proprietor A.P.Poulose. By Adv. Sri.C.R.Sivakumar Respondents/Complainant & Respondent 1 & 2 : 1 Food Safety Officer, Chelakkara Circle, Wadakkancherry, Thrissur District, Represented By The Public Prosecutor, High Court Of Kerala, Ernakulam, Pin- 682 031. 2 Mohandas C.C., S/O. Chandu, Chullivalappil House, Irunilam Code P.O., Mulloorkara-680 583, Thrissur District. 3 S.P. Kareem, S/O Sayed Pareed, Valiappat House, Btr Road Cochin-5, Licensee M/S Blue Mout Tea Dealers, 24/500 Essar Building. Gv Ayyar Road, Willington Island, Cochin-682003. Other Present: M/S Elavankudy Tea Co vs Food Safety Officer on 4 June, 2019 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/21759424/ 1 Sri Ajith Murali, Public Prosecutor",
    "facts": "This petition is filed under Section 482 of the Cr.P.C. 2. The petitioner herein, a Tea Company represented by its Proprietor, is the 4th accused in C.C. No.2564 of 2014 on the file of the Judicial First Class Magistrate Court, Wadakanchery. In the aforesaid case, the accused are being proceeded against for having committed offence punishable under Sections 3(1) (zz) (v) & (xi), 26(1), 26(2)(i) and 59(i) of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 and Rules 2.1.3.4(iii)(c) and Regulations 2.10.1.1. of the Food Safety Standards (Food Products Standards & Food Addictives) Regulations, 2011. It is submitted that on 02.11.2017, Annexure-A3 order has been issued by the Food Safety Standards Authority of India calling upon the Commissioners of Food Safety of all States/Union Territories to refrain from launching prosecution for non-confirmation of limit of iron fillings in respect of cases where samples were picked up or tested prior to 19.05.2016. In the very same order, the officers were advised to withdraw all prosecutions launched prior to 19.05.2016, either under the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 or under the Prevention of Food Adulteration Act, 1954.",
    "arguments": "3. It is submitted by the learned counsel appearing for the petitioner that the 3rd accused in the aforesaid case had approached this Court and by Annexure-A4 order, the entire proceedings were [LEAKAGE_MASK].",
    "petitioner_arguments": "3. It is submitted by the learned counsel appearing for the petitioner that the 3rd accused in the aforesaid case had approached this Court and by Annexure-A4 order, the entire proceedings were [LEAKAGE_MASK].",
